    "blurb": "The concert shines with a fiery Playin' → China Doll → High Time suite and strong Althea and Big River in the first set. Jerry delivers shredding solos while Phil locks in tight bass lines; the second set stays energetic through Wharf Rat, The Wheel and an uplifting encore.",
    "review": "Providence Civic Center on April 27, 1984 delivered a quintessential mid‑‘80s Dead experience. Kicking off with Alabama Getaway and rolling into Row Jimmy, the first set built momentum that culminated in a searing Althea and a big‑river romp where Jerry was described as “shredding” and Phil’s bass runs were called “monsterous.” The real highlight arrived in Set 2: a seamless Playin' → China Doll → High Time sequence that many reviewers called “tight” and “beautifully played,” propelling the band into an inspired stretch of The Wheel, Wharf Rat and a rousing Johnny B. Goode before closing with Touch of Grey. Jerry’s tone and vocal delivery remained on point throughout, Brent’s keyboards added just the right sparkle (“Brent crushes it”), and Mickey’s cerebral drumming gave the Space/Jam sections a dual‑drum depth that kept the energy soaring.\nOverall, the show is praised for its buoyant pacing, tight interplay, and memorable jams—making it a must‑listen snapshot of the Dead in their prime.",
